<title>THAILAND: Italian-Thai invests in transit system.</title>
<headline>Italian-Thai invests in transit system.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai construction firm Italian-Thai Development Plc said on Friday it had signed an agreement to invest 5.2 billion baht in Bangkok Transit System Co Ltd (BTSC).</p>
<p>BTSC, a unit of property developer Tanayong Plc, is building an elevated electric train sytem in the Thai capital. Italian-Thai is already undertaking constuction work on the project.</p>
<p>Italian-Thai said in a filing to the Stock Exchange of Thailand that it agreed to buy 65.21 million shares, or an 8.6 percent stake, in BTSC at 15.8 baht each.</p>
<p>Italian-Thai said it will also spend 4.2 billion baht on buying convertible debentures from BTSC.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 252-9950</p>
